  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding from Alaska Medicaid Skyrizi (risankizumab-rzaa), Version 1. Original 12/11/2024; Accepted 01/17/2025; Effective 03/1/2025. The references-page footer still says Accepted pending / Effective pending; dated approval pages govern this metadata.",
    "Closed indication labels represent FDA indication severity and systemic therapy or phototherapy candidacy for PsO. All four indications are adults (age \u226518). Phototherapy candidacy does not permit receiving concurrent phototherapy.",
    "Specialty gap: no prescriber specialty requirement in this Alaska PDF. No latex or hypersensitivity-to-risankizumab denial is specified; none is added.",
    "All four indications require trial and failure of a TNF blocker plus at least one other therapy; PsO includes at least one topical agent. No minimum trial duration is specified.",
    "Indication-gated categorical activity attestations: PsO PASI \u226512 (or equivalent); PsA one or more listed clinical manifestations plus baseline HAQ-DI (or equivalent) submitted, without a numeric threshold; CD baseline CDAI submitted and \u2265220; UC baseline mMS (or equivalent) submitted and \u22655.",
    "Initial authorization (notes only): monitoring plan; previous therapies and nature of failure; complete medication regimen; requested dosing conforms to an FDA-approved regimen by indication. Documentation requires manual review.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization approval up to 12 months. No separate reauthorization clinical criteria are specified in this PDF.",
    "Manual review: PS/PsA: 150 mg SC at week 0, week 4, then every 12 weeks. CD: initial 600 mg IV at weeks 0/4/8; maintenance 180\u2013360 mg SC at week 12 then every 8 weeks. UC: initial 1200 mg IV at weeks 0/4/8; maintenance 180\u2013360 mg SC at week 12 then every 8 weeks. Use the lowest effective maintenance dose for CD/UC. Route, dosing and quantity are not numerically enforced.",
    "Cautions (notes only): evaluate for tuberculosis (TB) before initiating treatment; avoid active TB. Monitor liver function tests (LFT), alkaline phosphatase and bilirubin during IBD treatment. Live vaccines are not recommended.",
    "PDL context: all SKYRIZI rows are non_preferred / OFF in CYTOKINE AND CAM ANTAGONISTS. Preferred peers without packs include Humira, Hadlima and Rinvoq (notes only). Infliximab has a separate partial class pack with product-specific PDL status in its notes. Linked alternatives require indication-specific review and do not imply confirmed coverage.",
    "This pack remains partial: initial documentation, reauthorization duration, monitoring, cautions, dosing and quantity enforcement require manual review."
  ],
